00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,010
Listen to a talk on environmental conservation.

2
00:00:03,010 --> 00:00:07,220
Let’s talk the environmental issue that has to do with how common household products have changed.

3
00:00:07,220 --> 00:00:11,921
More and more products contain bacterial killing chemicals these days.

4
00:00:11,921 --> 00:00:16,059
These antibacterial chemicals aren’t just in product like soap.

5
00:00:16,059 --> 00:00:18,553
They are in all sorts of household cleaners and toothpaste.

6
00:00:18,553 --> 00:00:22,045
And if you think about it for second you will realize that most of

7
00:00:22,045 --> 00:00:24,290
those chemicals just end up going down the drain.

8
00:00:24,290 --> 00:00:27,898
But you are probably thinking that all that stuff go through a treatment plan

9
00:00:27,898 --> 00:00:28,929
that removes chemicals, right?

10
00:00:28,929 --> 00:00:32,279
After all that’s what happens to stuff that goes down the drain

11
00:00:32,279 --> 00:00:34,038
Well, waste water is treated,

12
00:00:34,038 --> 00:00:37,908
but that doesn’t usually remove all the chemicals in it.

13
00:00:37,908 --> 00:00:42,130
The chemicals left in the treated water get into the aquatic environment.

14
00:00:42,130 --> 00:00:43,777
That is into the rivers,

15
00:00:43,777 --> 00:00:47,070
and streams where plants and fish and other animals live.

16
00:00:47,070 --> 00:00:51,668
Now to find out the affect of antibacterial chemicals on fresh water ecosystems, a

17
00:00:51,668 --> 00:00:53,310
study was done with algae,

18
00:00:53,310 --> 00:00:55,280
which are tiny plant like organisms.

19
00:00:55,280 --> 00:01:00,384
Different spices algae were taken to a lab and the expose to just a

20
00:01:00,384 --> 00:01:04,030
few antibacterial chemicals found in the streams. And guess what?

21
00:01:04,030 --> 00:01:08,548
In the experiment, the overall gross of algae and the number of spices dropped.

22
00:01:08,548 --> 00:01:11,130
This is not good and here is why.

23
00:01:11,130 --> 00:01:14,179
Algae are the base of the aquatic of food chain,

24
00:01:14,179 --> 00:01:17,227
which means that other organisms depend on them for food.

25
00:01:17,227 --> 00:01:21,496
So if the chemicals kill algae at the bottom of the food chain, the

26
00:01:21,496 --> 00:01:23,020
whole system is being disrupted.
